HST Office: VBA UserForms are written to .xlsm, .xls, .docm and .doc (owner request).

VbaExport wrote only the module streams, so a form became a document module and its dialog was
lost. oox/source/ole/vbaformexport writes the designer per MS-OVBA and MS-OFORMS from the Basic
dialog: a storage named like the module with \001CompObj, \003VBFrame, f (form and sites) and o
(control models); a Frame gets an iNN substorage and its controls back from the importer's flat
layout. Labels, text boxes, buttons, toggle buttons, check boxes, option buttons, combo and list
boxes, frames, spin buttons and scroll bars are written; other control types are left out.
- vbaexport: Package, BaseClass and Class lines in PROJECT, the MS Forms reference in dir, class
  and form module attributes, form captions in the code page check.
- axcontrol: combo box drop button and list rows are written.
- vbaproject: forms are read in the project's code page, not always Windows-1252, so Vietnamese
  form captions stay intact.
- vbaeventshelperbase: the event handler map is filled before it is stored. A document event on
  an .odt with a form crashed: looking up a handler loads the library, and the changes listener
  then erased the map entry being filled.
- docxexport, wrtww8: projects with forms are regenerated too, unless a control cannot be written
  (then the original project is kept as before).

